 features=(docs/'FEATURES.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('Neutral-site appearance keeps its native rules.','New verified Dynasty neutral plans use fanbase/prestige-based 30/70 to 70/30 splits; Play Now appearance remains native.')
 features+='\n## Prior private visitor-model changes\n\n- Prestige-based national support is separate from campus-distance travel demand. No added national component below 3.5 stars.\n- New home-site plans start at 3% or more visiting support; ordinary resistance limits most cases, and a genuinely struggling host/good national visitor can reach 35%. The common 5-15% range is a calibration target.\n- The strength slider still runs 0-200% and starts at 100%. It changes new plans only; 0 reaches the 3% starting minimum, not an empty visiting crowd. Neutral splits ignore this slider.\n- Small off-section parties use neighboring seat positions, separated from one another, with 1-8 supporters and most parties of 2-4. Bands and mandatory groups stay native.\n- Poor home seasons reduce ticket demand more strongly. Senior day contributes at most 4%, and combined routine event boosts are limited to 12%.\n- Ordinary severe-late-group games have a stable 65-75% capacity ceiling. FCS games and three-star prestige mismatches have stable 75-85% ceilings, with the requested opener/senior/night/rivalry/big-game exceptions. The lowest applicable limit wins, including over Fuller Crowds.\n- New home-site plans preserve a representative 1% visitor share among remaining modeled spectators through departures/temporary absences. No departed fan is restored. Empty-stadium modes and protected groups retain priority.\n- Prior plans keep their share, seed and old seating algorithm. Original visitor-plans.txt is not overwritten; new metadata lives in visitor-plans-v3.txt.\n- This is an offline-verified private candidate. Visual seating, native initial occupied denominators, live reload behavior and FPS are pending real-game review. No launcher-delay or touchdown-replay experiment is included.\n'
 features+='\n## Broadcast Universe compatibility trial\n\n- Recognizes the complete 0.7-beta1 post-play handoff selector. For a completed ordinary non-scoring gain at the configured full-screen threshold (12+ yards by default), lets the existing Standard Flow replay route run instead.\n- Smaller gains, touchdowns, turnovers, fumbles, special teams and unknown selector versions retain native handling. Both Additional Replays and Full-Screen Big Play Replays must be enabled. Existing offline scopes remain required.\n- A verified qualifying opponent gain also bypasses the complete early defensive inset shortcut to reach Standard Flow. Shorter gains retain that native inset. Bounded per-play replay-route logs identify pending evidence and selector outputs; these do not prove playback.\n- Insets retain their existing separate route. Native recording availability, presentation priority and user skipping still govern playback; the user reports successful full-screen replay testing with Broadcast Universe on 2.1.16; this is not a guarantee for every play.\n'
 features+='\n## Replay menu and performance\n\n- Restores Big Play Replay Minimum Yards under Broadcast in the Gameday settings tab. Range 10-60, default/reset 12 yards; saved thresholds are preserved. Legacy Replays INI values display correctly. All existing control IDs remain unchanged.\n- Crowd setup reuses exact seeded noise-grid hashes and geometry-only calculations. Neutral visitor layouts skip unused home-section scoring. Existing seat orders, fan parties and historical plans are preserved in identical-input fixtures.\n- The legacy diagnostic command file is checked once per second instead of ten times; gameplay callbacks, current diagnostic requests, sound, camera and replay timing keep their existing cadence.\n- Benchmarks measure offline generation, not live FPS or replay playback reliability.\n'
 features+='\n## Per-user storage trial\n\n- Settings, history, logs and verified runtime files now live under %LOCALAPPDATA%/Ace/DynastyCOT. All MMC copies share those module folders. No runtime writes are made to the installed Plugins folder.\n- Existing owned data is copied without deleting originals. Current AppData files win; differing imports are retained under Migration for review.\n'
 features+='\n## Home-crowd settling\n\n- Home leads of 18-42 points progressively soften the steady background, with a maximum 35% reduction; smaller leads and neutral sites are unchanged. Earned reactions keep their existing priority.\n- After a verified visiting touchdown, the home ambient layer retains its initial reaction, fades from 1.5 to 4 seconds, then stays subdued through the try and kickoff until the next ordinary possession.\n- The continuous native bed, chant and student-section buses settle too. These are shared buses, so the attenuation uses current visiting-supporter share as a listening proxy; this is not separately recorded home/away audio. Reaction, anticipation, sweetener, swell and band routing are unchanged.\n- Visiting cheers/sustained reactions are layered after the home background reduction. Home scoring or a real earned home reaction keeps priority. Neutral sites, simulated scores, stale results and unknown game contexts do not start a post-TD lull.\n- Pause/replay gaps suspend the timer; world/epoch changes, score corrections and disabled sound restore native behavior. The adjustment uses the existing verified native mixer and its fades, with no new hook or background polling.\n- Includes the earlier replay-threshold slider (default 12), exact-output crowd-preparation optimizations and shared AppData storage. Broadcast Universe full-screen replays have user-reported live success on 2.1.16; this new audio behavior still needs live listening.\n'
 features+='\n## Private Dynasty Extensions spring support\n\n- Verified PreSeason exhibition fixtures use the actual school native crowd palette throughout the ordinary seats. Protected groups remain native. No opposing visitor section, travel demand or visitor minimum applies.\n- Starting turnout is capped at 60% of verified capacity without raising a lower or empty native crowd. First-quarter competitive arrival adjustments are skipped.\n- First-half permanent exits remain at most 4%; thinning begins after native halftime and progresses toward 45-60% retention of the starting crowd at full time, independent of scores. Existing safe update windows and protected groups still limit visible changes. Temporary halftime absences follow the standard leave-and-return curve with a score-independent size, separate from the permanent wave.\n- Both offenses receive light, short result reactions from verified gains, first downs, touchdowns, sacks, stops and turnovers. Already playing native reactions take precedence. Added continuous roar, hostile escalation, volume boosts, camera motion and visiting-TD quieting are absent in spring. Existing replay policy and band routing are untouched. Native shared audio is not fully replaceable and still needs live listening.\n- Spring history adds Dynasty, school and fixture identities in attendance-history-v8.txt, leaving older attendance-history.txt untouched for rollback. Marker 250 and unverified roles retain native behavior.\n'
 features=features.replace('Marker 250 and unverified roles retain native behavior.','Unstamped marker250 and unverified roles retain native behavior. Stamped Extensions spring launches retain their existing recognition.')
 features+='\n## Spring crowd/fullness correction\n\n- Recoloring the spring crowd to the actual school can introduce new native clothing/body parts. Originally empty spectator positions now remain empty across those part changes, keeping visible attendance and the audio population denominator consistent.\n- The original native audience is frozen only after a completed baseline; generation, streaming and replay cannot refill those empty positions. Band/special protection and first callbacks for genuinely occupied positions are preserved.\n- Supporter counts exceeding their recorded original population are rejected by audio/reaction consumers rather than inflating fullness. No global gain, attendance history, native capacity or saved user choice is rewritten.\n- Retains the stamped spring fixture recognition, actual-school palette, 60% turnout ceiling, relaxed both-offense reactions, score-independent departures, regeneration menu and previous replay/performance/storage fixes. This correction still needs fresh-launch live visual/audio acceptance.\n'
