 (stage/'README.txt').write_text('GAMEDAY ATMOSPHERE by Ace - 2.1.24-spring-reactions1 PRIVATE TEST\n\nNot a public release. Built from the COT integration workspace.\n\nWhen you choose to test: close MMC and the game, back up the current GamedayAtmosphere.dll, then replace only that DLL in the versioned Mod Manager Plugins folder. Use one Gameday provider. Keep every data/settings/history folder. Restart MMC/game. Matching runtime files are embedded; no separate loader is added.\n\nNew crowd formulas apply to newly generated Dynasty fixtures. Older saved plans retain their old shares/layouts. A reused fixture will not demonstrate new tuning. The verified Dynasty loading handoff now allows up to two minutes without renewal, fixing slow launches. Other mode/fixture checks remain. The exact Broadcast Universe 0.7-beta1 ordinary post-play handoff now yields to the existing full-screen replay route on verified gains of 12+ yards (or your configured threshold). Short plays and excluded scoring/turnover/unknown cases retain native presentation. The replay yardage slider is restored under Gameday Atmosphere settings > Broadcast, with a 12-yard default and reset; existing saved values stay intact. Crowd preparation reuses repeated calculations while preserving seeded output. Launcher waiting and touchdown replay policy are unchanged. New audio: large home leads gently settle the steady background. After a verified visiting touchdown, the home ambient layer fades from 1.5 to 4 seconds and stays quieter through PAT/kickoff setup until the next normal possession; visiting cheers and earned reactions keep priority. Native shared continuous bed/chant/student buses are reduced without changing reaction or band routing. Neutral sites are unchanged. New audio requires live listening.\n\nNew plan metadata: %LOCALAPPDATA%/Ace/DynastyCOT/GamedayAtmosphere/History/visitor-plans-v3.txt. Original visitor-plans.txt stays untouched. To roll back, close MMC/game and restore your older DLL; keep all history files. Returning to this candidate can import missing older plans.\n\nData and logs: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ace\\DynastyCOT\\GamedayAtmosphere. Keep that folder during uninstall/rollback. Pre-storage releases still use their older data paths; originals are retained for those versions. See FEATURES.md and the comparison/testing report beside this ZIP. No live install, injection or publication was performed by the build process.\n',encoding='utf-8')
